{"The helper that copies `contexts.error_sampling.client_sample_rate` into `sample_rate` treats falsy values as \"missing\", so a valid value of `0` (or `\"0\"`) will be ignored and `sample_rate` will not be set, causing tests that rely on zero sampling to behave incorrectly": 0.7665380835533142, "The cache key for error upsampling eligibility uses Python's built-in hash of the project ID tuple, which is randomized per process; this makes cache keys non-deterministic across workers and prevents consistent reuse and invalidation of cached eligibility results across the system": 0.9808869361877441, "The upsampling eligibility check incorrectly uses the outer `dataset` instead of the `scoped_dataset` actually being queried, so when `_get_event_stats` is called with a split dataset (e.g. `discover` vs the original metrics dataset), `is_errors_query_for_error_upsampled_projects` evaluates against the wrong dataset and can skip or misapply upsampling for split error queries": 0.9731438755989075, "The function for upsampled counts uses a raw `Column(\"sample_weight\")` instead of `self.builder.column(\"sample_weight\")`, bypassing the builder's field/alias resolution and entity prefixing; this can cause Snuba queries to fail or reference the wrong column when the underlying dataset uses table aliases or field aliases for `sample_weight`": 0.9681578874588013}